From: Muchun Song <muchun.song@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:18:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm/hugetlb: fix validation of unsupported HugeTLB orders

Commit 7ce6048d3a7d ("loongarch: drop ranges for definition of
ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER") removed the ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER ranges for
LoongArch.  Besides dropping unreasonable upper limits, this allowed
values below the architecture defaults.

With 16KB pages, LoongArch defaults ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER to 11, matching
HUGETLB_PAGE_ORDER.  Forcing it to 10 while enabling HugeTLB permits
order-11 HugeTLB folios even though MAX_FOLIO_ORDER is 10.  LoongArch does
not select ARCH_HAS_GIGANTIC_PAGE, so this violates the generic MM
assumption that folios cannot exceed MAX_PAGE_ORDER.

This invalid configuration is accepted by Kconfig.  BUILD_BUG_ON_INVALID()
does not reject it either because it only checks whether the expression is
valid and never evaluates the comparison.  Detection is left to the
runtime warning in hugetlb_add_hstate(), after earlier boot paths may
already have used the invalid configuration.

When an invalid HugeTLB order can be identified at build time, reject it
there.  Otherwise, reject it at runtime before the mismatch propagates
further.  Use MAYBE_BUILD_BUG_ON() so constant violations fail the build
while dynamically determined orders are checked at runtime.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/20261104071858.757793-1-songmuchun@bytedance.com
Fixes: 7ce6048d3a7d ("loongarch: drop ranges for definition of ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER")
Signed-off-by: Muchun Song <muchun.song@linux.dev>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/sashiko-outbox-192874@kernel.org/
Suggested-by: Huacai Chen <chenhuacai@kernel.org>
Reviewed-by: Huacai Chen <chenhuacai@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Oscar Salvador <osalvador@suse.de>
Tested-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>
Cc: Kiryl Shutsemau <kas@kernel.org>
Cc: Mike Rapoport <rppt@kernel.org>
Cc: WANG Xuerui <kernel@xen0n.name>
---
 mm/hugetlb.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/hugetlb.c b/mm/hugetlb.c
index 5c2741b07e559..cb2de24affdc4 100644
--- a/mm/hugetlb.c
+++ b/mm/hugetlb.c
@@ -4197,7 +4197,6 @@ static int __init hugetlb_init(void)
 
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof_field(struct page, private) * BITS_PER_BYTE <
 			__NR_HPAGEFLAGS);
-	BUILD_BUG_ON_INVALID(HUGETLB_PAGE_ORDER > MAX_FOLIO_ORDER);
 
 	if (!hugepages_supported()) {
 		if (hugetlb_max_hstate || default_hstate_max_huge_pages)
@@ -4205,6 +4204,8 @@ static int __init hugetlb_init(void)
 		return 0;
 	}
 
+	MAYBE_BUILD_BUG_ON(HUGETLB_PAGE_ORDER > MAX_FOLIO_ORDER);
+
 	/*
 	 * Make sure HPAGE_SIZE (HUGETLB_PAGE_ORDER) hstate exists.  Some
 	 * architectures depend on setup being done here.
-- 
